   <indicator ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of national strategies implemented</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline year="2022"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-04-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-06-30"></period-end>
     <target value="4">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">4 - Afghanistan, Angola, Iraq and Sri Lanka</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="1">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">GICHD visited Baghdad in June 2022 and organised a four-day strategy implementation plan workshop. All relevant national and international stakeholders were brought together to agree on activities to reach the  outcome targets until the end of 2023 in Iraq&apos;s new national mine action strategy 2022-2028. Several donors (including the Netherlands) participated in the workshop closure. 

GICHD also co-organised a donor meeting with the Dutch at the Embassy of the Netherlands in Baghdad, with five international donors participating. GICHD provided an update on the strategy process and the workshop and participants discussed key challenges moving forward,  including donors&apos; priorities, future funding and coordination with DMA and IKMAA.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-10-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="4"></target>
     <actual value="1">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Iraq&apos;s National Mine Action Strategy is being implemented by all relevant stakeholders, using the framework and process facilitated by GICHD in June 2022.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-09-30"></period-end>
     <target value="4"></target>
     <actual value="1">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Iraq 2022-2028 National Mine Action Strategy is currently being implemented by all relevant stakeholders, using the framework and process facilitated by GICHD in June 2022.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
