    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-03-31"></period-end>
     <target value="4">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">4 - Afghanistan, Angola, Iraq and Sri Lanka</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual value="1">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sri Lanka&apos;s severe financial and political crisis since May last year resulted in a delay in the government approving the strategy. GICHD had several meetings with Embassies and the Government to try to encourage the approval of the strategy.

&#x200B;&#x200B;&#x200B;&#x200B;The strategy was approved by the Minister of Housing and Urban Construction on 28 March. GICHD supported the Government of Sri Lanka with organising the high-level launch in Colombo on 30 March. The launch was well attended, including by several ministries from the Government of Sri Lanka (Ministry of Health, Ministry of Foreign Affairs and NMAC) international donors (the High Commissioners of Canada and the UK, the Swiss Ambassador and representatives from Japan, Norway, Australia and Switzerland). Representatives from all operators (HALO, MAG, DASH and SHARP), the SLA HDU (Sri Lanka Army humanitarian demining unit)  and the SLCBL (Sri Lanka campaign to ban landmines) also participated in the event.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
